# Manmabot V1 — Logic Gaps To-Do

GUI features are largely in place. Items below are **main-logic gaps**: settings that save/show but do not drive the live bot, or engine behaviors that are still missing.

Check items off as you complete them.

---

## 1. Schedule executor

The schedule UI saves tasks and labels timing as Draft. Nothing runs tasks by clock.

- [ ] Build a schedule executor (pick due task → apply settings → start → stop on window/duration)
- [ ] Honor `enabled`, `start_time` / `end_time`, `duration_minutes`, `time_mode`
- [ ] Honor `repeat_daily` and `weekdays`
- [ ] Switch to the next due task when the current one ends
- [ ] On Apply / Start: use the task’s `account_id` **and** its server / character slot for login (not only the account store defaults)
- [ ] Align task `character_slot` with autologin (accounts currently allow slots 1–3)

---

## 2. Settings → runtime adapter

`apply_runtime_settings()` only copies a subset of fields into `Profile`. Wire every control you treat as a real feature, or remove/hide it from the UI.

### Already applied (reference — leave checked)

- [x] Class, map, selected farms, farm rotate timer
- [x] Species levels / blacklist
- [x] HP potion %, escape HP/MP %
- [x] Spell slots, heal-until-HP, mana reserve
- [x] Arrow buy quantity
- [x] Loot `all_items` / `adena_only`, adena-weight threshold, humanize, game language

### Still decorative / ignored

- [ ] Hunt: attack mode (ranged / magic / melee)
- [ ] Hunt: attack range, keep distance, close attack
- [ ] Hunt: MP-above spell, spell count, ranged count, fallback melee
- [ ] Hunt: hunt route, hunt radius, transit route
- [ ] Hunt: return on weight / no supplies / potion NPC
- [ ] Deduplicate Hunt “return HP/MP” vs Recovery escape % (one source of truth)
- [ ] Recovery: “Use HP potion” toggle
- [ ] Recovery: resurrect if dead
- [ ] Recovery: resume after relogin
- [ ] Recovery: max retries (drive `RecoveryBudget`, not hardcoded 3/10 min)
- [ ] Recovery: random teleport enable + HP threshold
- [ ] Magic: per-class skill checkboxes (sunlight, glowing aura, bounce attack, …)
- [ ] Magic: disable-in-combat, stop-below-MP
- [ ] Equipment: buy arrows on/off, normal vs silver, silver qty
- [ ] Equipment: repair, restock potions, equip profile
- [ ] Other: loot mode `adena_weighted` (accepted by UI, rejected by adapter)

---

## 3. Town / bag loop

Arrow buy exists. Full supply cycle does not.

- [ ] Shop sell when bag is full (explicitly not implemented today)
- [ ] Repair equipment trip
- [ ] Restock potions trip
- [ ] Return to town / safe on high weight (HUD weight only forces adena loot today)
- [ ] Return on no supplies
- [ ] Honor chosen potion / shop NPC from settings
- [ ] Implement or remove `PlayerMode.TRADING`

---

## 4. Combat policy

Live combat is sticky click/cast + give-up + species rules. Hunt tab policies are not implemented.

- [ ] Attack mode selection actually changes behavior (not only character class)
- [ ] Keep-distance / kiting
- [ ] Attack-range gate for bow / melee / magic
- [ ] Mage: spell-then-melee (or ranged) fallback when MP is low
- [ ] Royal-specific combat (currently knight clone)
- [ ] Elf-specific combat policy beyond Mother Tree + click cadence

---

## 5. Recovery & session lifecycle

Engine already potions, retreats, teleports, respawns, and can relogin — but Recovery toggles do not control it.

- [ ] Gate HP potions on the Recovery toggle (+ hotbar mapping)
- [ ] Gate death → restart click on “resurrect if dead”
- [ ] Gate auto-relogin on “resume after relogin”
- [ ] Pass Recovery max retries into `RecoveryBudget`
- [ ] Random teleport at configured HP (not only fixed ~10% idle emergency)
- [ ] Allow Start when game is already in-world **without** requiring an account (optional / advanced)
- [ ] Pass task server + character slot into `AutoLoginRequest`

---

## 6. Content & maps

- [ ] Ship dungeon map packs named in UI (`talking_island_dungeon_F1`, `desert_dungeon_F1`) **or** remove those names from the map list
- [ ] Ensure dungeon packs include terrain / `patrol.yaml` so patrol mode can run
- [ ] Confirm mainland + talking_island nav assets are complete for pathfinding

